course: dictionary
lesson: 399
title: Apparently: heard or seen?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Apparently is a small word with two jobs. It can mean «I have heard this, but I am not sure it is true». It can also mean «it looks like this, though it may not be so».
explain: «Ravens have been filmed sliding down snowy roofs, apparently for fun.» The writer has heard or read this, and passes it on. Apparently warns you that this is what people say, not something the writer has checked.
explain: «The gentlemen say: "Here is a poor old thing, a washerwoman apparently, who has fainted in the road!"» The gentlemen only judge by how she looks. Apparently tells you that she seems to be a washerwoman, which may not be the truth.
explain: «Toad lay amidst the ruins of the chairs, apparently completely satisfied.» Toad looks happy, but the word hints that this may only be how it seems. When you meet apparently, ask: is this news I heard, or how something looks?
fact: Apparently means according to what people say, or as it seems.
fact: «Apparently, we're getting a new teacher» means someone said so, but nobody has proved it yet.
fact: Apparently often comes at the start or in the middle of a sentence, with commas around it.
fact: In stories, apparently can hint that something is not what it seems.
fact: A good check is to swap in «it seems» or «I have heard» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: Ella says, «Apparently, the pool is closed today.» What does apparently tell you? | *Someone said so, and Ella is not sure it is true | Ella has checked the sign and is certain | Ella is swimming today | The pool is closed for ever
exercise: «The gentlemen say she is a washerwoman, apparently.» What does apparently show? | She is a famous queen | She has been proved to be a washerwoman | She is a ghost | *It is how she looks to them, which may not be the truth
exercise: Which word in «Ravens have been filmed sliding down snowy roofs, apparently for fun.» hints that this is only what people say? | roofs | *apparently | snowy | ravens
test: Grandad says, «Apparently, it will snow on Sunday.» What is the best meaning? | *I have heard it will snow, but I am not certain | It will snow, and I have seen the proof | It is snowing right now | Snow is my favourite thing
test: Which sentence shows that something only seems true? | I like apples. | Two plus two is four. | The sun is hot. | *The shop looked empty, apparently, but the lights were on in the back room.
exam: Which word could replace apparently in «Apparently, the bus is late», keeping the same meaning? | Never | Certainly | *Reportedly | Quickly
